## Dashboard pipeline

See `.cursor/rules/orders-dashboard-refresh.mdc` for the build steps. Short version:
1. `python3 src/polygon/build_gains_from_orders.py` — Orders.csv → gainsandlosses_enriched.csv
2. `python3 src/polygon/build_trade_dashboard_data.py` — enriched CSV → trade_dashboard_data.json
3. `python3 scripts/serve_pnl_calendar.py` — serves large_cap_pnl.html + tradezilla_dashboard.html
4. Shortcut: `npm run orders:live` (rebuild + serve) or `npm run orders:refresh` (rebuild only)

Default Large Cap rebuild filters: `--same-day-only --from-date 2026-08-19`.

## Compliance review pattern

When asked to critique or review trades:
1. Read `TRADING_PLAYBOOK.md` for the rules
2. Read the orders file (Orders.csv or a specific date range CSV)
3. Check each trade against: OT-OCO usage, position size, hold time, stop width, time window, reversal count
4. Present as a Canvas with day-by-day breakdown and rule grades
